WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for t1-02-anger-alchemy.mp3 — machine-transcribed on-device from the existing audio (SR-472). Not proofread.
NOTE Cues with ids phase-recognise/-regulate/-release/-rise mark where each step begins; js/saferise-poster.js reads them.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.310
A boundary was crossed,

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:06.530
Not a mild annoyance, not a transient bad mood.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.510
A line was breached and something inside you surged to defend it.

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:19.845
This process does not demand immediate calm. Fire cannot be commanded to cool
on queue, and forcing tranquillity right now is why attempts to handle anger

00:00:19.845 --> 00:00:22.260
usually collapse in the first ten seconds.

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:32.240
Keep moving if you need to move, hold still if you are already still.

00:00:32.640 --> 00:00:35.070
Your position stands exactly where you set it.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:45.690
No one is here to placate you or talk you out of your stance.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:58.170
The physical surge hits like a reflex, while the clearer awareness that knows
what to do takes a moment to catch up.

00:01:04.550 --> 00:01:08.290
Most of your energy gets burned in the friction between those two speeds.

00:01:08.850 --> 00:01:12.330
Four distinct stages, let's move through them step by step.

phase-recognise
00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:26.280
Recognise your physical self-registered this breach long before your conscious
mind finished formulating a response

00:01:26.820 --> 00:01:29.050
Locate the heat intention right now.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:32.210
Look to the clenching in your jaw, the tight fists.

00:01:32.650 --> 00:01:35.080
The stiffness extending down the back of your neck

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:36.990
Or the flash across your face.

00:01:43.830 --> 00:01:46.330
Give this physical activation a single word.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:47.390
Adjutated.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:50.020
Notice what that single word leaves out.

00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:54.860
It excludes the other person, their name, their expression, what they did.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.980
And the entire devastating argument you have assembled to throw back at them.

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:07.040
That isn't because your grievance is wrong.

00:02:07.440 --> 00:02:12.580
Your position may be completely justified and it will remain just as valid
when we finish.

00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.550
But there are two separate dynamics occurring right now.

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.300
And only one of them is within your immediate reach.

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:26.350
The case against the moustatic.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:31.730
But the physiological charge in your jaw and hands is dynamic and capable of
shifting.

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.590
Go one layer deeper.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:41.600
Beneath the heat

00:02:41.810 --> 00:02:44.650
Something vital was treated as though it had no worth.

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:47.670
A boundary of yours or someone you care for.

00:02:53.450 --> 00:02:57.490
Anger arrives precisely where respect or safety was compromised.

00:02:57.930 --> 00:03:00.490
Look closely at the primary driver underneath.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:09.729
Losing control over your own trajectory, being left isolated to carry the
wreckage, taking on the burden of being the failure, or running out of time

00:03:09.729 --> 00:03:10.740
for what matters.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:21.840
Sink into that core vulnerability, leave it right where it is.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.850
Nothing needs to be solved here.

phase-regulate
00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:35.770
Regulate, now we shift your physical posture to handle this surge without
breaking.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:43.370
Draw a breath in for four counts.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.200
And let it out for 6 counts.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:55.180
Keep the exhale longer than the inhale every single time.

00:04:02.410 --> 00:04:05.690
Your breathing naturally wants to go short, shallow and sharp.

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:15.830
Acknowledge that impulse but choose a longer rhythm anyway

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.550
If your hands are clenched into fists,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:24.540
It's open them.

00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.870
Stretch your fingers wide, then let them drop loose.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:33.010
Shift your awareness out of your jaw and anchor it directly into the center of
your chest

00:04:39.380 --> 00:04:41.580
The heat may spike before it settles.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:51.217
That is a normal clearing response, not a failure, thoughts will keep firing.
Let each one arrive without grabbing it, arguing with it, or taking it to its

00:04:51.217 --> 00:04:51.880
conclusion.

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:54.890
An arising thought is simply neural noise.

00:04:55.120 --> 00:04:57.040
It is not a command to strike back.

00:05:02.980 --> 00:05:07.020
If you notice yourself striving to meditate correctly, soften your effort.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:13.450
Striving is just another form of fighting, weather passes through a room, but
the room never becomes the storm.

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:24.320
Consider the internal trial running on repeat in your mind.

00:05:24.670 --> 00:05:25.610
You know the script

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:31.020
You deliver the opening blow, they respond, and you return with a sharper
counter.

00:05:31.410 --> 00:05:34.180
You have probably rehearsed it five times already.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.790
Notice how every single run ends.

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:44.500
Every time

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:53.650
That isn't self-delusion. The part of your mind constructing that conversation
is fiercely loyal to you. It's entire job is protection.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.250
So it naturally hands you the winning lines.

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:04.150
But every single pass through that mental arena re-arms your nervous system,
reigniting the flame all over again.

phase-release
00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:10.800
Release

00:06:11.320 --> 00:06:13.340
The underlying anger stays

00:06:13.820 --> 00:06:14.770
It is yours

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.880
It was earned and no one is taking it from you.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:31.970
But you can lay down the mental rerun, just the rerun. Ask yourself this
question.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:34.460
What was this force built to protect?

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:45.660
Anger moves forward with momentum while fear retreats

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:47.960
Angus steps up to meet the threat.

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:53.330
It surfaced because a boundary was breached, pulling you upright to defend
what matters.

00:06:53.780 --> 00:07:02.630
On its own terms, it fulfilled its primitive job, realizing this doesn't
excuse anyone's behavior or dissolve your boundaries.

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:12.220
Keep the question, it will serve you when your body settles.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.950
Some of this heat belongs to today.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:17.550
Some may belong to older breaches.

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:26.820
You don't need to sort them out right now.

00:07:27.110 --> 00:07:28.660
Admit the harder truth.

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:32.140
A part of you doesn't want to let this heat go.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:39.330
That makes sense.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.100
It feels like armor.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.730
It is the force that prevents you from being compromised.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:49.110
And your system remembers what happened on the days you didn't have it.

00:07:49.460 --> 00:07:52.340
But that defense was built with older tools.

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:57.470
The vigilant part of you doesn't realize you have better options now.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:08:08.271
No one is asking you to stand down your guard, only to realize that the person
standing here today is far more capable than the one who first built that

00:08:08.271 --> 00:08:08.680
armor.

00:08:14.830 --> 00:08:20.800
Place that underlying vulnerability directly into your breath stream and let
it be.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:32.470
None of this gets settled from inside the fire.

phase-rise
00:08:32.790 --> 00:08:33.450
Rise.

00:08:33.810 --> 00:08:36.760
Finally, we step into deliberate authority.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:49.590
Visualize yourself from across the room, your set, replaying the argument,
consumed by the heat.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:59.850
You are furious and you have every right to be.

00:09:07.070 --> 00:09:12.480
Now picture the version of yourself you want to embody the next time a
boundary is crossed

00:09:13.210 --> 00:09:14.620
Same heat rising

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:16.660
Same impulse to strike.

00:09:22.430 --> 00:09:27.840
But you are the one choosing where your power goes, not on winning a fleeting
argument.

00:09:28.060 --> 00:09:30.540
But on safeguarding what actually matters.

00:09:36.620 --> 00:09:37.910
Where are you standing?

00:09:38.230 --> 00:09:41.890
What does your voice sound like when it is completely steady?

00:09:42.130 --> 00:09:44.540
What are the exact words you use?

00:09:52.660 --> 00:09:59.750
Step directly into that composure. The anger is still present, but your focus
is where you choose to place it.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:03.430
Pick one concrete response you will use next time.

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.430
Afterwards, record what shifted.

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.860
Take one last slow breath.

00:10:15.160 --> 00:10:24.330
In for four and out for six, feel the solid floor supporting you, gently move
your hands and feet and open your eyes when you are ready.

00:10:24.710 --> 00:10:29.180
Return to this anchor whenever you need to forge strength from fire.
